{"team":"DET","col":"#4FA8E8","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":63.3,"adot":6.5,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p>They're a heavy under-center team (48% shotgun vs ~68%) \u2014 a pro-style, run-committed structure.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>In the passing game the ball funnels to <strong>Amon-Ra St. Brown</strong> \u2014 <strong>29% of targets</strong> (league ~23%), a genuine alpha share that concentrates the receiving value at the top.</p><p>Their backs are a real part of the passing game \u2014 RBs see <strong>22%</strong> of targets (vs ~18%), which props up <strong>Jahmyr Gibbs</strong>'s reception floor.</p><p>It's a short, rhythm-based passing game \u2014 aDOT just <strong>6.5</strong> \u2014 that lives on YAC and checkdowns, boosting reception totals over big-play yardage.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 59% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 48% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>50%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Jahmyr Gibbs</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 45 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They give up deep shots (24% of throws travel 15+ vs ~19%) \u2014 big-play WR upside against them.</p><p>They surrender <strong>109 rushing</strong> and <strong>249 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.63/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.29/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comebac